Verified correct, no action. _first_overlap plus list_view's node.name sort already yields the lexicographically greatest survivor for equal leaf sets, and a four-part stem is a strict string prefix of its five-part counterpart, so legacy loses to new; unit 4's "production change only if a test fails" is right and pinning it anyway is right. _seq_prefix (split("-")[:2]) is shape-agnostic, so five-part names disturb neither write_nap nor surgery.py's seq-prefix lookup. Path.stem grouping in list_view handles five-part names because the tag contains no dot. Both committed stores (.summem/naps and dogfood/.summem/naps) hold four-part pairs, so unit 7's dogfood step has real work, and no test reads this repo's own store, so rewriting it is safe. release-please-config.json and tests/test_version.py enumerate summem and surgery.py only, so a version-less migrate.py introduces no lockstep failure. Stem length lands at 121 plus grain digits, matching the issue's count.

Radical innovation (advisory, not blocking, plan deliberately not changed). Collapse the nap pair into one file. A nap today is {stem}.tree plus {stem}.summ, and a large share of this plan's surface exists only to keep those two byte-consistent: the "one atomic pair" invariant, migrate.py renaming both suffixes together, the scan for a stem whose .tree and .summ came from different variants, leaf_digests returning None on a half pair, and migrate.py's incomplete-pair skip. This change already breaks the disk format and already rewrites every pair on disk, so the same breath could make a nap one file: {seq}-{leafset}-{grain}-{digest}.nap holding {"sum": caption, "tree": {...}}, with the tag being the digest of that one file's bytes. Mismatch becomes unrepresentable instead of test-enforced, _unlink_node and list_view's stem-grouping dict both halve, and migrate.py becomes a merge-and-rename rather than a paired rename. The cost to weigh: it discards a deliberate property, since a conflict-marked caption currently degrades wake while the payload stays clean and zoomable, and a corrupt single file would take the payload down with it. It also rewrites _nap_caption, list_view, wake degradation, and every missing-or-dirty-caption test (test_view.py lines 22 and 55, test_caption_conflict.py line 75).
